# Files this repo deliberately does NOT carry from its template.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. Every repo in this tree merges from a `stem` remote. A file
# that a descendant has deleted is not a settled decision as far as git is
# concerned: the next time the template TOUCHES that file, the cascade stops
# with a modify/delete conflict, and whoever is running it has to work out from
# scratch whether the deletion was deliberate.
#
# Listing the path here does not change what git does - the conflict still
# happens - but it makes the answer a lookup instead of an excavation, and
# `scripts/apply-omissions.sh` turns the resolution into one command.
#
# FORMAT. One path per line, relative to the repo root. `#` starts a comment.
# Give every entry a reason: the next person's question is never "which file",
# it is "why", and an unexplained list is how a deletion outlives the reason for
# it and becomes cargo cult. A DIRECTORY entry covers everything under it, which
# is usually what you want - a whole replaced directory rather than forty files -
# but name one only when the whole directory is what you replaced, because the
# entry also asserts that nothing under it exists.
#
# THREE GUARDS, all pointing different ways:
#
#   web/test/offshoot-omissions.test.ts   every LISTED path is still absent
#   scripts/check-omissions.mjs           every ABSENT path is listed (needs the stem)
#   scripts/apply-omissions.sh            re-drop them all, and run both checks
#
# ENTRIES ARE STEM-RELATIVE: what belongs in a repo's list is what IT drops from
# ITS OWN stem. A descendant must never copy its template's entries down, because
# those paths are already absent from the branch it merges and so cannot be
# omissions there. This file is the one file in the set that is per-repo DATA
# rather than shared machinery: when a cascade conflicts on it, the descendant's
# entries win, always.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE MACHINERY LIVES AT `template-svelte`, THE ROOT OF THIS TREE, and cascades
# down from there. The other three files named above are byte-identical at every
# node, with one stated exception inside `apply-omissions.sh` for the two repos
# that also run a dangling-import check. It was written twice before that, once
# on each branch of the tree, and the two copies had diverged into two variants
# of `check-omissions.mjs` within the week - identical in behaviour, nineteen
# lines apart in what they claimed. An ancestor is the distribution point for
# shared machinery even when it has nothing of its own to guard; the alternative
# is that divergence-by-copy, which is measured rather than feared.
#
# WHAT AN EMPTY LIST MEANS, AND IT IS NOT THE SAME THING AT EVERY NODE. At
# `template-svelte` this file can never hold an entry: the root has no stem
# (`fanout.config.json` there says `"stem": null`), so there is nothing above it
# to omit FROM, and `check-omissions.mjs` run there correctly refuses rather than
# reporting a pass it did not earn. Its emptiness follows from the shape of the
# tree and needs no measuring. ANYWHERE ELSE an empty list is a claim about this
# repo, and checking it is one command:
#
#   git fetch stem <branch> && node scripts/check-omissions.mjs FETCH_HEAD
#
# "This repo omits nothing" is allowed to stand only when that command says so.
# The last file in this tree to assert it without running anything was wrong by
# seventeen paths, and a cascade had already paid for it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THE MIDDLE GUARD ABOVE HAD TO BE WRITTEN, from this repo's own record.
# The middle one is the one that had to be written, and why is worth knowing.
# THIS FILE USED TO SAY "this template omits nothing - it is where the files come
# from", which was false: this repo is a descendant of template-svelte-shadcn like
# any other, and it drops three inherited paths. The other two guards are blind to
# that, because a path nobody listed and a path that never existed look identical
# from inside one repo. Measured across this tree on 2026-09-25, EVERY list was
# incomplete - this one 0 of 3, template-commit-reveal 0 of 17, reveal-or-die 4 of
# 52, bleeps 1 of 21, mandalas 2 of 24 - and one cascade had already paid for it.
# See the finding of that date on the `work` branch.

web/src/lib/Head.svelte
# REPLACED, not dropped: the same component is `web/src/lib/core/metadata/Head.svelte`.
# It moved because it reads the document's location to build a canonical URL, and
# in `core/` it cannot ask the framework for that - it takes the
# `documentLocation` CAPABILITY instead, which the layout provides. That is the
# whole point of the boundary ADR-0005 draws.
#
# This one is already documented in a second place, deliberately:
# `web/test/framework-boundary.test.ts` explains that the stem carries a
# KNOWN_LEAKS entry for this path and this repo does not need one, BECAUSE of the
# move above. That note is about the leak list; this entry is about the file. Both
# are true and the cascade meets them at different moments.

web/static/icon.png
# This repo has its own logo and it is a VECTOR: `web/static/icon.svg`, from which
# `pnpm generate-pwa-icons` renders every raster the PWA needs into `static/pwa/`
# (favicons, maskable icons, apple-touch). A single stem-supplied png is both the
# wrong artwork and the wrong format.
#
# MIND THE STALE SCRIPT THIS LEFT BEHIND, which is a real thing to trip over:
# `web/package.json` still carries the stem's `generate-pwa-icons-and-tags`,
# spelled `pwag static/icon.png ...`, so running it fails on a missing file. This
# repo's `prepare` was re-pointed at the svg script and the old one was never
# removed. Recorded rather than deleted here because a script is code and this is
# a list; see the finding on the `work` branch.

